# EAN Studio — Agent Guidelines

## 1. Project Context & Stack
- Retail barcode inventory and price check suite.
- `index.html`: Client mobile scanner PWA running in browser / Capacitor.
- `admin.html`: Local management console for store PC (operates with C:\1C\Scaner).
- Tech: Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, CSS3, WebRTC P2P, HiveMQ MQTT (WebSocket), File System Access API.

## 2. Hard Constraints (DO NOT VIOLATE)
- NO external backend servers or cloud databases. Data persistence is strictly local (`localStorage` and local CSV via File System Access API).
- DO NOT rewrite, simplify, or refactor MQTT broker connection or WebRTC peer negotiation logic unless explicitly instructed.
- DO NOT add external build tools (Vite, Webpack) or complex NPM dependencies. Keep files self-contained.
- Always preserve CSV parsing logic (support both comma `,` and semicolon `;` delimiters, handle BOM headers).
- Always maintain offline resilience and error handling for camera permissions and MQTT reconnects.

## 3. Workflow & Code Style
- Perform surgical edits: modify only the requested function or DOM element without altering unrelated code.
- Always check for potential edge cases (network drops, invalid barcodes, missing DOM IDs) before implementing.
- Before editing large blocks, explain the planned approach briefly.

## 4. Communication & Language
- Always interact, explain changes, and respond to the user in LATVIAN (latviski).
- Write Git commit messages and user documentation in Latvian.
- Code variables and comments in code should remain in clean English.